Do not dereference a frame's fence when GLFence::Create() returned null.

The browser dies on the HarmonyOS emulator before it can paint: SIGSEGV at
address 0 on the Chrome_InProcGp thread, inside

  gl::GLSurfacePresentationHelper::GetFrameTimestampInfoIfAvailable
  gl::GLSurfacePresentationHelper::CheckPendingFrames
  gl::GLSurfacePresentationHelper::ScheduleCheckPendingFrames

PreSwapBuffers takes the fence branch on gl_fence_supported_ and stores
whatever GLFence::Create() returns, without checking it. The emulator
advertises the extension, so IsSupported() is true, but Create() fails at
runtime and the frame is queued with a null fence.

CheckPendingFrames already handles frames with no timing source, but its
early-out tests gl_fence_supported_, not the frame, so it does not fire here.
The frame reaches GetFrameTimestampInfoIfAvailable, whose only protection is a
DCHECK that this build compiles out, and the final branch dereferences the
null fence.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/gl-null-fence.patch

diff --git a/ui/gl/gl_surface_presentation_helper.cc b/ui/gl/gl_surface_presentation_helper.cc
--- a/ui/gl/gl_surface_presentation_helper.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/gl_surface_presentation_helper.cc
@@ -97,10 +97,19 @@
     int64_t end = 0;
     frame.timer->GetStartEndTimestamps(&start, &end);
     *timestamp = base::TimeTicks() + base::Microseconds(start);
-  } else {
+  } else if (frame.fence) {
     if (!frame.fence->HasCompleted())
       return false;
     *timestamp = base::TimeTicks::Now();
+  } else {
+    // GLFence::IsSupported() can report true while GLFence::Create() still
+    // fails, and PreSwapBuffers stores the null it hands back. The early-out
+    // in CheckPendingFrames tests gl_fence_supported_ rather than the frame,
+    // so such a frame arrives here with nothing to wait on. The DCHECK above
+    // catches it in a debug build; a release build dereferenced the null and
+    // took down the GPU thread on the first swap. Report the frame as
+    // presented now instead -- there is no timing source to do better with.
+    *timestamp = base::TimeTicks::Now();
   }
   // Below logic is used to calculate final values of timestamp, interval and
   // flags when using timer/fence to report the timestamps.
